    "id": "rate_half_list_budget_three_fiber_two_cycle_c2_one_antipodal_product_ratio_trace_compiler",
    "title": "Budget-three fiber-two c=2 one-antipodal packets have a product/ratio trace compiler",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For a one-antipodal c=2 denominator {1,-1,c,d}, put P=cd, t=c/d, and Z=t+t^-1. Then X=(c+d)^2=P(Z+2). Complementary-root torsion is equivalent to the coupled half-order circuit P_39^2=1 and Z_39=2P_39 under repeated squaring/trace doubling. The primary packet is therefore an exact (P,Z) circuit with distinctness (Z^2-4)(1+P^2-PZ)!=0 and no square-root gate. The trace Z always lies in F_p; in the reciprocal quadratic chamber P^p=P^-1. The compiler does not prove the circuit empty or address antipodal-free C2-PAR.",
